#. type: Title ###
#: ../../info/wxmaxima.md:93
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "Command autocompletion"
msgstr "Megjegyzés kiválasztása"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../../info/wxmaxima.md:96
#, no-wrap
msgid "_WxMaxima_ contains an autocompletion feature that is triggered via the menu (Cell/Complete Word) or alternatively by pressing the key combination <kbd>CTRL</kbd>+<kbd>SPACE</kbd>. The autocompletion is context-sensitive. For example, if activated within a unit specification for ezUnits it will offer a list of applicable units.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../../info/wxmaxima.md:98
msgid "![ezUnits](./ezUnits.png){ id=img_ezUnits }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../../info/wxmaxima.md:100
#, no-wrap
msgid "Besides completing a file name, a unit name, or the current command or variable name, the autocompletion is able to show a template for most of the commands indicating the type (and meaning) of the parameters this program expects. To activate this feature press <kbd>SHIFT</kbd>+<kbd>CTRL</kbd>+<kbd>SPACE</kbd> or select the respective menu item (Cell/Show Template).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: ../../info/wxmaxima.md:101
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "Greek characters"
msgstr "Unicode karakterek"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../../info/wxmaxima.md:104
msgid "Computers traditionally stored characters in 8-bit values. This allows for a maximum of 256 different characters. All letters, numbers, and control symbols (end of transmission, end of string, lines and edges for drawing rectangles for menus _etc_.) of nearly any given language can fit within that limit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../../info/wxmaxima.md:106
msgid "For most countries, the codepage of 256 characters that has been chosen does not include things like Greek letters, though, that are frequently used in mathematics. To overcome this type of limitation [Unicode](https://home.unicode.org/) has been invented: An encoding that makes English text work like normal, but to use much more than 256 characters."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../../info/wxmaxima.md:108
msgid "_Maxima_ allows Unicode if it was compiled using a Lisp compiler that either supports Unicode or that doesn’t care about the font encoding. As at least one of this pair of conditions is likely to be true. _WxMaxima_ provides a method of entering Greek characters using the keyboard:"
msgstr ""

